# Course fairness invariants

Two properties make this a race rather than two unrelated runs. Both are enforced
structurally. Changes in `lane.py`, `patterns.py` or `reset_game` must preserve them.

## 1. Both lanes must generate identical courses from one seed

Every spawn position and timing comes from `self.rng`, the `random.Random` a lane
owns. Seeding two lanes identically makes their courses byte-identical.

- **Never call the global `random` module from lane or spawn code.** Anything else
  in the process consuming randomness would shift the sequence and destroy
  reproducibility. Always `self.rng`.
- **Never draw from `self.rng` conditionally on player state.** Two lanes must make
  the same number of draws in the same order regardless of how each player is doing,
  or the courses diverge partway through a round.
- New spawn timers, new jitter, new pattern parameters: all `self.rng`.
- `reset_game` draws one seed and passes it to both lanes. Do not give lanes
  separate seeds, and do not reseed mid-round.
- Keep `Lane.update()` taking `target_y` as a parameter rather than holding a
  `Player` reference. That decoupling is why a lane can be simulated with no player
  at all, which `tools/pick_course_seeds.py` requires.

## 2. Every spawned pattern must be provably flyable

`pattern_is_passable()` sweeps a candidate in 8px columns and requires an opening of
at least `ZAPPER_MIN_GAP_H` in every one. `_spawn()` re-rolls up to 8 times, then
falls back to a short floor beam that cannot wall the lane off by construction.

- **Every new zapper pattern goes through this check.** Do not add a builder whose
  output bypasses `_spawn()`.
- Do not trust authored numbers instead of the check. The check immediately caught a
  real case: two facing emitter nodes each eat half a node's width, so a gap authored
  at 84px left only 64px free.
- Column step must stay well under the player's height so no beam slips between
  samples.
- Keep the fallback trivially safe. It is the last line of defence and must not be
  able to block a lane.

Adding a coin formation or zapper pattern is a builder function plus one tuple
entry in `patterns.py`. Nothing in `lane.py` should need to change.

## Telegraphs are safe by construction, not by a flag

- A `MissileWarning` has no `rect()` and no `collides()`, and the `Missile` is not
  constructed until the warning elapses. Do not give the warning a hitbox, and do
  not pre-create the missile "disabled."
- A telegraphing `SeekingMissile` is excluded from `Lane.hazards()` by state.
- Scientists are excluded from `hazards()` entirely — they are a reward and must
  never damage the player. Their absence is intentional and documented; do not
  "fix" it.

If you change `COURSE_SEEDS`, regenerate it with `tools/pick_course_seeds.py` rather
than hand-editing. Its `PCT_LO`/`PCT_HI` are the difficulty dial.
